  "notes": "Gothic: a steep gabled front with a pierced barge-board, a traceried oriel over a pointed porch, patterned tiling in two colours. Two doors are stated rather than inferred - the parlours communicate by folding doors, and 'a door opening out of the hall excludes the steam etc. from the kitchen, which damages furniture, and, rising to the bed-rooms, damps and injures the linen'. The plate carries the same note as the text about building it in pairs: put the W.C. under the stairs, the coal cellar in its place, and light the hall by a window over the roof of the coal-cellar. The back bed-room divides into two on the dotted lines, which is not counted here because the plate draws it whole.",
